{"output":"I’ll trace ownership checks in job transitions and lock renewal, patch the source, then build and run the supplied regression tests with Node 24.\n\nThe Lua checks test only whether a lock exists, not whether its token matches. That lets stale workers release or replace another owner’s lock. I’ll restore token comparisons while preserving the administrative “0” bypass, and move delayed-job promotion after retry ownership validation so rejected retries emit no events.\n\nThe build passed on Node 24. The test command did not start because the shell rejected its log redirection; I’ll rerun it without redirection. I’ve also added a regression test covering recovery, stale transitions and renewals, unchanged Redis state, and successful completion by the replacement owner.\n\nAll 268 existing tests passed. The new test failed during setup because it used the removed queue.client getter. I’ll switch it to the repository’s Redis-client helper and rerun it.\n\nFixed token validation for job transitions and single/batch lock renewal. Rejected retries now avoid delayed-job promotion. Administrative bypass remains intact.\n\nVerification on Node 24:\n- npm run build passed.\n- All 268 supplied regression tests passed.\n- Added ownership regression test passed after correcting its setup.\n- git diff --check passed.\n\nNo existing tests or configuration changed.","final_output":"Fixed token validation for job transitions and single/batch lock renewal. Rejected retries now avoid delayed-job promotion. Administrative bypass remains intact.\n\nVerification on Node 24:\n- npm run build passed.\n- All 268 supplied regression tests passed.\n- Added ownership regression test passed after correcting its setup.\n- git diff --check passed.\n\nNo existing tests or configuration changed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":27,"tool_calls":[{"name":"shell","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"g